import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Patio Privacy Planner" description="Create a patio privacy worksheet with a spatial boundary preview, example screen counts, optional cost arithmetic, and a practical checklist."><header class="container page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Free planning tool · No account needed</p><h1>Patio Privacy Planner</h1><p class="lead">Choose a starting approach for more privacy, visualize an example screen layout in 3D, and save a checklist before you buy.</p></header><section class="container section planner-layout"><form class="panel planner-form" id="privacy-form" novalidate><fieldset><legend><span>1</span> Measure your space</legend><label for="space">Outdoor space</label><select id="space"><option value="patio">Ground-level patio</option><option value="balcony">Balcony</option></select><div class="field-pair"><div><label for="patio-width">Outdoor width (ft)</label><input id="patio-width" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="1" data-max="100" value="10" required/></div><div><label for="depth">Outdoor depth (ft)</label><input id="depth" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="2" data-max="100" value="8" required/></div></div><div class="field-pair"><div><label for="width">Width to screen (ft)</label><input id="width" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="1" data-max="100" value="6" required/></div><div><label for="screen-height">Target height (ft)</label><input id="screen-height" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="1" data-max="10" value="6" required/></div></div><p class="small">Plan one straight boundary. Height is a preference to research, not a safe-height recommendation. Measure from the seating position you want to protect.</p></fieldset><fieldset><legend><span>2</span> Choose an approach & check the site</legend><p class="small">Your priority changes the advice. Wind exposure and balcony permission determine which checks come first. These choices do not change the module count.</p><label for="need">What matters most?</label><select id="need"><option value="view">Block a direct sightline</option><option value="flex">Easy to move or store</option><option value="green">Add greenery</option></select><label for="exposure">Wind exposure</label><select id="exposure"><option value="exposed" selected>Exposed or unsure</option><option value="sheltered">Sheltered; product limits still apply</option></select><label class="check-label"><input type="checkbox" id="approved"/> For a balcony, I have confirmed permission, permitted loads, drainage, and wind restrictions with building management.</label></fieldset><fieldset><legend><span>3</span> Compare an example layout</legend><label for="panel-width">Usable width per example module (ft)</label><input id="panel-width" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="1" data-max="10" value="3" required/><p class="small">Use an actual product's usable width if known. The default is a paper-layout assumption, not a product recommendation. Supports and overlaps may change fit. Use a decimal point or comma (for example, 2.16 or 2,16).</p><details class="cost-details"><summary>Optional: estimate using your own prices</summary><label for="module-price">Price per module (USD)</label><input id="module-price" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0" data-max="100000" placeholder="Leave blank if unknown"/><label for="extra-cost">Additional costs (USD)</label><input id="extra-cost" type="text" inputmode="decimal" data-min="0" data-max="100000" value="0"/><p class="small">Include supports, delivery, or taxes in additional costs. No prices are retrieved from retailers.</p></details></fieldset><div class="plan-actions"><button class="button" type="submit">Create my plan →</button><button class="reset-button" type="reset">Start over</button></div><p class="small">Your answers stay in this page. Nothing is sent to us or stored automatically.</p><noscript><p>JavaScript is needed for the interactive worksheet. Read our <a href="/articles/patio-privacy-ideas-for-renters/">patio privacy guide</a> for the planning steps.</p></noscript></form><section class="panel planner-result" aria-label="Your patio privacy worksheet"><h2>Your privacy plan</h2><div id="results" role="region" aria-label="Planner results" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" tabindex="-1"><div class="planner-empty"><p class="eyebrow">Example only · 10 × 8 ft patio</p><div id="planner-preview" aria-label="Example spatial layout"></div><h3>See where your screening would go.</h3><p>The floor shows your outdoor width and depth. The upright modules show an example screen along one boundary — including the height you enter.</p><div class="preview-key"><span><i class="key-floor"></i>Outdoor floor</span><span><i class="key-screen"></i>Example screening</span></div><p class="small">This example has two 3-foot modules, covering a 6-foot target. Create your plan to replace it with your measurements. Support footprints, furniture, and safe installation are not modeled.</p></div></div></section></section><section class="container planner-guidance"><h2>What this tool does</h2><p>It compares starting approaches and calculates straight-line example coverage. It does not select or test products, determine required supports, assess wind or loads, check building codes, or guarantee privacy at a particular height.</p><p>Read the <a href="/articles/patio-privacy-ideas-for-renters/">patio privacy guide</a> or <a href="/articles/small-patio-furniture-layout/">small patio layout guide</a> before making changes.</p></section><script type="module" src="/assets/planner.js?v=spatial-20261014" is:inline></script></Base>
